      "clinical_time": "2124-08-01T09:27:14",
      "available_time": "2124-08-05T18:19:11",
      "content": "Left lower lobe pulmonary nodule with calcification, considered a benign lesion; tiny right pulmonary nodules; scattered linear opacities in both lungs; focal calcification of the aortic wall. Mass in the lower outer quadrant of the right breast; incidental fatty liver and an intrahepatic hypodense lesion; enlargement of the left thyroid lobe, with bilateral hypodense thyroid nodules and calcified foci. Please correlate with clinical findings and other relevant examinations and follow up.\nSeveral nodular opacities are seen in both lungs: a solid nodule is seen in the posterior basal segment of the left lower lobe (SE203, IM133), with a long diameter of approximately 16mm and a calcified focus within. A solid nodule is seen in the medial segment of the right middle lobe (SE203, IM96), with a long diameter of approximately 3mm. A solid nodule is seen in the anterior basal segment of the right lower lobe (SE203, IM101), with a long diameter of approximately 3mm. Scattered linear opacities are present in the right middle lobe and lingular segment of the left upper lobe. The density of both lower lobes is heterogeneous. No abnormalities are seen in either hilar region. The visualized tracheobronchial shadows are normal. No abnormally enlarged lymph nodes are seen in the mediastinum. Focal calcification of the aortic wall. A mass is present in the lower outer quadrant of the right breast, with a long diameter of approximately 20mm. Incidental fatty liver and an intrahepatic hypodense lesion. Enlargement of the left thyroid lobe, with bilateral hypodense thyroid nodules and calcified foci.",
